{{also|take out}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|take out}}
* {{l|en|take-out}}

===Etymology===
From the verb phrase ''take out''.

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|North America}} (Of food) intended to be [[eaten]] off the [[premises]] from which it was bought.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|takeaway}} {{q|chiefly Britain, Australia and New Zealand}} 
* {{l|en|to carry-out}}, {{l|en|to-go}} {{qualifier|Scotland and some dialects in the U.S. & Canada}}
* {{l|en|takeaways}} {{q|New Zeland}}
* {{l|en|grab and go}}

